sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor learner as You
  participant command as Workload command
  participant control as Anyscale control plane
  participant operator as Anyscale operator
  participant api as Kubernetes API
  participant head as Ray head on AKS
  participant managed as GPU worker on managed AKS
  participant flex as Ray worker on Flex
  participant storage as Azure Blob Storage

  learner->>command: Run run-anyscale-workload with CPU or GPU mode
  command->>api: List Ready nodes and allocatable CPU and memory
  api-->>command: Return capacity for the selected node pools
  command->>command: Reserve headroom and write the compute config
  command->>control: Submit compute config and Ray Job
  operator->>control: Poll outbound for pending operations
  control-->>operator: Return the Anyscale workload operation
  operator->>api: Create Ray cluster and job resources
  api-->>head: Schedule the head pod in Region A
  alt CPU mode
    api-->>flex: Schedule one CPU worker on aksflexnodes
    head->>flex: Start one-worker CPU training
    flex-->>head: Return loss and runtime metrics
  else GPU mode
    api-->>managed: Schedule one GPU worker in Region A
    api-->>flex: Schedule one GPU worker on aksflexnodes
    Note over managed,flex: The same Unbounded network spans AKS and Flex pod traffic
    head->>managed: Start rank 0 or rank 1
    head->>flex: Start the other training rank
    loop Four smoke training steps
      managed-->>head: Return rank loss and runtime metrics
      flex-->>head: Return rank loss and runtime metrics
    end
  end
  head->>storage: Write and read workload-summary.json with managed identity
  command->>control: Poll job state and read driver logs
  control-->>command: Return SUCCEEDED and WORKLOAD_SUMMARY_JSON
  command->>api: Collect Kubernetes pod placement
  command-->>learner: Save joined dual GPU training proof
